{
 "sources": {
  "trend": "OECD PISA 2025 Results (Volume I), Table I.B1.2d.10 — difference in SCIENCE performance by immigrant background, PISA 2015 / 2018 / 2022 / 2025, before and after accounting for socio-economic status and language spoken at home. https://stat.link/6gtbnx",
  "cycle2022": "OECD PISA 2022 Results (Volume I), Tables I.B1.7.17, I.B1.7.21 and I.B1.7.29 — mathematics, reading, and the within-immigrant language gap. https://stat.link/qmuad8"
 },
 "retrieved": "2026-09-20",
 "cycles": [
  "2015",
  "2018",
  "2022",
  "2025"
 ],
 "outcomes": {
  "science.raw": {
   "label": "science gap",
   "basis": "trend",
   "note": "immigrant minus non-immigrant mean science score."
  },
  "science.escs": {
   "label": "science gap, after socio-economic status",
   "basis": "trend",
   "note": "the same gap with socio-economic status accounted for."
  },
  "science.escsLang": {
   "label": "science gap, after status and home language",
   "basis": "trend",
   "note": "the same gap with socio-economic status AND language spoken at home accounted for. The closest thing here to a gap that is not about composition."
  },
  "maths": {
   "label": "mathematics gap (2022 only)",
   "basis": "cycle2022",
   "note": "immigrant minus non-immigrant mean mathematics score. Mathematics was the major domain in 2022."
  },
  "reading": {
   "label": "reading gap (2022 only)",
   "basis": "cycle2022",
   "note": "immigrant minus non-immigrant mean reading score."
  },
  "homeLanguage": {
   "label": "within-immigrant language gap (2022 only)",
   "basis": "cycle2022",
   "note": "among immigrant students: those who speak the language of assessment at home minus those who do not. Positive means speaking it at home is an advantage."
  }
 },
 "caveats": [
  "TWO BASES, NEVER MIXED. The science series comes from a trend table that recomputes every cycle on one comparable basis; the 2022 maths, reading and language figures come from that cycle's own tables. Checked against each other on 2022 science, 20 of 71 countries differ by more than a score point and the worst by 4.4 — small, real, and reason enough to keep the series apart rather than splice them.",
  "Science was the major domain in PISA 2025 and mathematics in 2022. A minor domain is measured less precisely.",
  "countryCode is resolved once here, offline, against the national units of the eal map. The app never matches on names at runtime.",
  "join = \"sub-national only\" marks a country PISA reports nationally that this atlas holds only as sub-national units (Belgium, the United Kingdom, Hong Kong). Joining a national outcome to one region's policy would be wrong, so these carry no countryCode.",
  "Taken from the StatLink workbooks, not the PDFs: pdftotext misaligns these tables badly enough to pair a country with another country's numbers."
 ],
